    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/Technician-at-the-Neuroinformatics-Research-Group/1453014933/": {
      "title": "Technician",
      "description": "Technician at the Neuroinformatics Research Group Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » At the University of Vienna, a community almost 11,000 individuals, including approximately 3,000 dedicated to administration and organization, passionately pursuing answers to the profound questions that shape our future. As bridge builders, they connect diverse worlds, promote transparency and accuracy and foster an open exchange across disciplines and working cultures. Interested? We are currently seeking a/an Technician at the Neuroinformatics Research Group 39 Faculty of Computer Science Job vacancy starting: 12/01/2026 | Working hours: 40.00  | Classification CBA: §54 VwGr. IIIb Limited contract until: Job ID: 6411 Long Description The Neuroinformatics Research Group (FG NI) is a small, international and interdisciplinary team within the Faculty of Computer Science. We develop AI methods to understand the relationships between brain activity, behaviour and consciousness and to use these insights to derive new therapeutic approaches for neurological disorders. We offer a diverse working environment with room for your own ideas and foster a culture of mutual respect and appreciation. The position is initially limited to one year. A permanent may be offered subsequently. Long Description Your personal sphere of influence: In this position, you will manage our laboratory for electroencephalography (EEG) measurements and support the team in conducting experimental studies. You will ensure the reliable operation of the existing measurement and experimental hardware, maintain it, and, as needed, further develop it in coordination with the team. In addition, you will work on the maintenance and further development of the group's internal IT infrastructure. This includes managing the hardware and software in use and assisting employees with IT-related issues. Long Description Your future tasks: Managing and further developing our EEG lab Providing support in conducting experimental studies Developing, adapting, and testing hardware and software tools Procuring and replacing hardware and software Installing, configuring, and maintaining hardware and software equipment, particularly PC workstations, printers, and other IT components First-level support for the research group’s staff Network administration Website management for the research group in collaboration with our administrative assistant Contribution to managing the shared IT infrastructure of the Department of Computer Science, such as Linux servers (e.g., file servers or CI/CD servers), as well as the internal video conferencing infrastructure Long Description Your profile: Completion of a general or vocational secondary school Professional experience in system administration, support, development, management Professional experience in the technical support of an EEG laboratory (or willingness to familiarize yourself with this subject area) Excellent written and spoken German and English Excellent knowledge of Linux, Windows, and macOS Good programming skills in Python, MATLAB, C/C++, and Java A structured, goal-oriented, and independent work style Ability to work in a team and, ideally, experience in working with research groups Good knowledge of web programming Knowledge of the design and construction of electronic circuits is an advantage We are looking for a new team member who shares our values of openness, transparency, clear communication, and mutual respect, and who will contribute to a successful collaboration. Long Description What we offer: Work-life balance: Flexible working hours and – as far as the job allows it – the option to work remotely. Inspiring working environment: A small, diverse, and dedicated team in a university research setting with a relaxed and supportive working atmosphere. Space for creativity: Management of the EEG lab, the experimental measurement and study infrastructure, and the group’s internal IT systems. Opportunity to contribute your own ideas and technical solutions to further develop these areas in collaboration with the team. Collaborative teamwork: Friendly and respectful interaction within an interdisciplinary team, as well as regular networking with technicians from other research groups. Good public transport connections: Your workplace is easily accessible by public transport. Internal further training: A comprehensive and free range of professional development opportunities to deepen your skills. Fair salary: The basic salary of EUR 3,131.30 (employment group IIIb) on a full-time basis (14 times a year) increases if we can credit your professional experience. Equal opportunities for everyone: We welcome every new personality to the team! How to apply: With CV and letter of motivation Via our job portal via the \"Apply now\" button If you have any content questions, please contact: Moritz Grosse-Wentrup moritz.grosse-wentrup@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of  Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection Application deadline: 11/22/2026 IT Apply now » Find similar jobs: IT, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) T