    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-Assistant-postdoctoral/1452443133/": {
      "title": "University Assistant postdoctoral",
      "description": "University Assistant postdoctoral Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » The University of Vienna is a community of almost 11,000 individuals, including approximately 7,700 academic staff members, who passionately pursue answers to the profound questions that shape our future. Fueled by curiosity and a deep sense of duty, they contribute invaluable insights to research and teaching, enriching our society. Are you inspired and driven by the desire to make a meaningful impact? We are currently seeking a/an University Assistant postdoctoral 45 Faculty of Philological and Cultural Studies Job vacancy starting: 11/01/2026 | Working hours:  40.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 lit. b (postdoc) Limited contract until: 10/31/2032 Job ID: 6365 Explore and teach at the University of Vienna, where over 7,500 brilliant minds have found a unique balance of freedom and support. Join us if you’re passionate about groundbreaking international research and academic excellence. Ready to be part of our team? Let’s shape the future together! We would be happy to welcome you in our team until 31.10.2032. Your personal sphere of play: Your future position will be at the Institute for European and Comparative Linguistics and Literature, in the Department of Comparative Literature. This department is distinguished by its excellent research in the fields of memory studies, world literature, ecological research in literary and cultural studies, as well as intermedial and interdisciplinary narrative studies. The Department of Comparative Literature supervises approximately one thousand students and is actively engaged in research, teaching, and the communication of scholarship through European and international exchange. It operates at the intersection of languages and literary forms and examines the role of literature and poetic forms —even beyond the arts in the narrower sense—for the present, the past, and the future. Your future tasks: You will actively participate in research, teaching, and administration, which means: Development of an independent research profile in the field of comparative cultural studies, with a focus on the environmental humanities or the field of literature and knowledge. Contribution to research projects and scholarly studies in the fields of applied comparative studies, digital humanities, and literary theory. You will publish internationally and give presentations. Application for projects and secure external funding. Preparation and completion of a habilitation thesis ready for publication. You will independently teach courses in accordance with the provisions of the collective bargaining agreement. Supervision of your students’ theses. Performance of administrative tasks related to research and teaching. Active involvment in building a scientific communication network for comparative literature projects. This is part of your personality: Completed doctoral/PhD degree in General and Comparative Literature, Philology, or Cultural Studies Outstanding dissertation demonstrating proven expertise in literary studies or literary theory Research competence and initiative demonstrated through international publications in peer-reviewed journal Experience in research management Teaching skills / experience in e-learning IT skills (e.g., website development, database maintenance) The following traits and skills would be a welcomed addition: Knowledge and experience in the field of science communication Experience living abroad Experience in advising students Excellent English skills (C1) / knowledge of at least one other foreign language Team player with strong social and communication skills What we offer: Work-Life Balance: You’ll have flexible working hours and can also work remote (by arrangement). Inspiring Work Environment: You’ll be part of an international team with excellent research infrastructure in a relaxed work environment. Good Public Transportation Access: Your new workplace is easily accessible by public transportation. In-house training and coaching: We offer you ongoing opportunities to deepen your skills. Choose from a free selection of over 600 workshops per year. Fixed-term contract and fair salary: The base salary of EUR 5,014.30 (paid 14 times a year, based on full-time employment) from November 1, 2026, to October 31, 2032, will increase if we can take your professional experience into account. Equal opportunities for all: We welcome every new member to our team! That's how easy it is to apply: Submit your academic resume / letter of intent Submit your list of publications Submit a summary of your main research areas (max. 1 page) Contact details of references Proof of completion of your doctoral/PhD program Via our job portal / “Apply Now” button If you have any questions, please contact: Solvejg Elisabeth Nitzke solvejg.nitzke@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection ​Application deadline: 11/30/2026 Post Doc Apply now » Find similar jobs: postdoctoral, Postdoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing, and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled AddThis Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider AddThis Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
