    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-assistant-predoctoral/1452430833/": {
      "title": "University assistant predoctoral",
      "description": "University assistant predoctoral Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » University assistant predoctoral At the University of Vienna almost 11,000 personalities work together towards answering the big questions of the future. Around 7,700  of them do research and teaching, around 3,000 work in administration and organisation. We are looking for a/an University assistant predoctoral 45 Faculty of Philological and Cultural Studies Job vacancy starting: 01/01/2027 | Working hours: 30.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc) Limited contract until: Job ID: 6389 Explore and teach at the University of Vienna, where more than 7,700 academics thrive on curiosity in continuous exploration and help us better understand our world. Does this sound like you? Then join our accomplished team! The Department of German Studies at the University of Vienna is the largest research and education center dedicated to all aspects of the German language and German-language literature. The deparment´s five core areas are Modern German Literature, Older German Language and Literature, German Linguistics, German as a Foreign and Second Language, and German Language Education. These are complemented by the interdisciplinary fields of Gender Studies, Cultural Studies, Literary Theory, and Children´s and Young Adult Literature. The department serves more than 5,000 students. Your opportunities in this role: As a Predoctoral University Assistant, you will contribute to research projects in the field of Older German Language and Literature, with a particular focus on the High and Late Middle Ages and the transition to the Early Modern period. The position is offered for a total period of four years. The employment contract will initially be limited to 18 months and will be automatically extended to four years unless the employer issues a notice of non-renewal within the first 12 months. Your specific responsibilities: You will actively contribute to research, teaching & administration. In particular: You will participate in our wide range of research activities in the field of Older German Language and Literature. You will be expected to conclude your doctoral thesis agreement within 12-18 months. You will work on your doctoral dissertation in the field of Older German Language and Literature. You will independently teach courses in accordance with the provisions of the collective bargaining agreement. You will undertake administrative duties related to research and teaching. Your qualifications and personal qualities: A completed teacher-training degree or master´s degree in German Philology, with a specialization in Older German Language and Literature or German Medieval Studies A doctoral research project in the field of Older German Language and Literature Teaching skills and/or experience with e-learning A team-oriented approach and strong interpersonal and communication skills What we offer: Work-life balance: You will benefit from flexible working hours and the option to work remotely for part of your time. Inspiring working atmosphere: You will be part of an international team with outstanding research infrastructure and relaxed working atmosphere. Excellent public transport connections: Your new workplace is conveniently accessible by public transport. Internal training & coaching: We offer ongoing opportunities to expand and deepen your skills. Fair salary: The basic salary of EUR 3.836,10 per month on a full-time basis and may increase if relevant professional experience can be credited. Get off to a great start in your new job: the Welcome Compass helps you settle into your new role at the University of Vienna and life in Vienna. Equal opportunities for everyone: We welcome every new individual who adds to our team! How to apply: Please submit: Your academic CV and a compelling letter of motivation A summary of your research interests, previous experience - including courses taught, internships, projects, and similar activities - and your doctoral research proposal (maximum four pages) Official confirmation of completion of your master´s or diploma degree and your degree certificates If available, a list of publications and evidence of teaching experience Your application via our  job portal using the \"Apply now\" button For questions about the position, please contact: Coralie Rippl-Uhlenhut coralie.rippl-uhlenhut@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of  Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection Application deadline: 11/12/2026 Prae Doc Apply now » Find similar jobs: predoctoral, Praedoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website