    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/Senior-Scientist-in-Atmospheric-Data-Assimilation/1452415933/": {
      "title": "Senior Scientist in Atmospheric Data Assimilation",
      "description": "Senior Scientist in Atmospheric Data Assimilation Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Senior Scientist in Atmospheric Data Assimilation At the University of Vienna more than 11,000 personalities work together towards answering the big questions of the future. Around 7,700 of them do research and teaching, around 3,000 work in administration and organisation. We are looking for a Senior Scientist in Atmospheric Data Assimilation 53 Faculty of Earth Sciences, Geography and Astronomy Job vacancy starting: 12/01/2026 | Working hours: 40.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 lit. b (postdoc) Limited contract until: Job ID: 6255 Explore and teach at the University of Vienna, where over 7,500 brilliant minds have found a unique balance of freedom and support. Join us if you’re passionate about groundbreaking international research and academic excellence. Ready to be part of our team? Let’s shape the future together! Your personal sphere of play: We are looking forward for an enthusiastic senior scientist to join the research group on “Numerical Weather Prediction (NWP) and Data Assimilation” at the Department of Meteorology and Geophysics ( https://img.univie.ac.at/en/research/nwp) . Our overall goal is to advance NWP and the understanding of atmospheric processes through: the assimilation of new observation types (e.g. cloud-affected satellite radiances and Aeolus wind lidar observations); improved data assimilation schemes; improved parametrizations via parameter estimation and uncertainty quantification; ensemble-based diagnostics for the analysis influence and forecast impact of observations. The candidate should propose a research topic that links to current activities of the group and complements our current research. Your future tasks: You actively participate in research, teaching & administration, which means: You conduct research on the proposed topic and develop new research ideas in collaboration with the research group; You disseminate the results in peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations, and are committed to the FAIR guiding principles for scientific data management; You contribute to project proposals and develop your own proposals; You teach independently in our BSc and MSc curricula within the scope of the provisions of the collective bargaining agreement; You support the other group members in scientific and technical concerns; You contribute to organizational and administrative tasks. This is part of your personality: PhD / Doctoral degree in meteorology, physics, mathematics or a related subject; Good communication skills and ability to work in a team; Profound programming skills; Experience in numerical modelling; Expertise in data assimilation; Excellent command of written and spoken English. What we offer: A postdoctoral contract with the perspective of a permanent position: You will have flexibility in conducting your own research and developing new research ideas and the chance to shape your research profile and establish yourself as a leading expert in the field. Inspiring and supportive working atmosphere: You will be part of an international team in a healthy and fair working environment with excellent research infrastructure. Work-life balance: You have flexible working hours and the option to partly work from home (within Austria) upon agreement. Good public transport connections: Your workplace is easily accessible by public transport. Internal further training & Coaching: Opportunity to deepen your skills on an ongoing basis. There are over 600 courses to choose from – free of charge. Fixed-term contract and fair salary: The gross salary of at least EUR 5014.30 (payable 14 times per year / amount as of 1 January 2026) increases if we can credit professional experience and allows for a comfortable life in a vibrant city with affordable housing prices and quick access to outdoors. Get off to a great start in your new job: The Welcome Compass helps you settle into your new role at the University of Vienna and life in Vienna. Equal opportunities for all: We welcome every additional/new personality to the team! The University of Vienna aims to become carbon neutral by 2030: We fully support low-carbon options for travelling. The position is available from December 2026 , but a later starting time is possible. The position is initially limited for three years with possibility to become permanent by mutual agreement. It is that easy to apply: Letter of motivation; Research plan; Curriculum vitae including a list of publications Names and contact details of two persons serving as references Via our job portal / Apply now - button. If you have any content questions, please contact: Martin Weißmann martin.weissmann@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities, the advancement of women and diversity . We lay special emphasis on increasing the number of women in senior and in academic positions among the academic and general university staff and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of  Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection Application deadline: 12/10/2026 (MM-DD-YYYY) (Senior) Lecturer & Researcher Apply now » Find similar jobs: Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies, (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E), (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing, and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled AddThis Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider AddThis Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
