      "title": "Senior Lecturer (academic and instructive teaching) part-time 20 hours per week",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer (academic and instructive teaching) part-time 20 hours per week Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Senior Lecturer (academic and instructive teaching) part-time 20 hours per week At the University of Vienna, almost 11,000 people work together on the big questions of the future. Approximately 7,700 of them are academic staff members. These are individuals who, with their curiosity and their continuous pursuit of excellence, engage in international cutting-edge research and teaching. With us, you will also find space to unfold your potential. We are looking for a/an ... Senior Lecturer (academic and instructive teaching) part-time 20 hours per week 50 Faculty of Life Sciences Job vacancy starting: earliest possible | Working hours:  20.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 lit. b (postdoc) Limited contract until: fixed-term contract for 4 years Job ID: 6195 The Department of Nutritional Sciences in the Faculty of Life Sciences at the University of Vienna is looking for a Senior Lecturer (m/f/d) in the field of biochemistry with a focus on nutritional sciences. The position is initially a fixed-term contract for 4 years . In case of positive evaluation at the end of the fixed-term period of 4 years, conversion to a permanent position is possible . The 20-hour-per-week workload includes a combination of academic and instructive teaching. Do you enjoy working with young people, are you curious, and do you want to share your knowledge? As a Senior Lecturer, you play a key role in educating students. In addition to providing a solid academic education, we also place a special emphasis on the development of students’ personal skills. We support students in developing a curious and problem-solving mindset, thereby creating a solid foundation for the professional challenges the next generation will face. Your workplace: The position is located at the Department of Nutritional Sciences, which is part of the Faculty of Life Sciences. The Department offers an interdisciplinary and scientifically diverse environment in which key issues at the interface of food, nutrition and health are addressed in both research and teaching. As a Senior Lecturer, you will primarily teach on the Bachelor’s and Master’s programs in the field of nutritional sciences, with a focus on biochemistry, and contribute to the further development of scientifically based, research-driven teaching. Our focus is on student-oriented, skills-based and research-driven teaching that links scientific findings with current societal challenges in the field of nutrition and health. The 20-hour-per-week position involves a teaching load of approximately 3 semester hours per week of academic teaching and approximately 8 semester hours per week of instructive teaching. Your future tasks: Planning, performing and further developing of courses in nutritional sciences with a focus on biochemistry (lectures, practical courses, seminars) at Bachelor’s and Master’s level Designing, organizing and supervising of laboratory practical courses, including instructing students in experimental techniques Ensuring laboratory and occupational safety (SOPs, safety briefings, quality standards, management of equipment and chemicals) Developing of innovative teaching and assessment formats (e.g. blended learning, e-learning, competence-based assessment) Contributing to the development of new (digitally aided) teaching concepts and to module coordination Providing subject-specific guidance to tutors and practical instructors Collaborating with teaching and research teams; carrying out administrative tasks related to teaching operations What we expect: We are looking for people who see university teaching as an interesting and challenging career field. Requirements for application are: A relevant university degree at master’s level or higher, including a PhD (e.g. nutritional sciences, biochemistry, molecular biology, food chemistry or a related discipline) Several years’ experience as a university lecturer, particularly in (bio)chemical and nutritional physiology laboratory practical courses Methodological expertise in biochemical and molecular biological techniques Research experience in biochemistry or related disciplines; publications or project experience Knowledge of health and safety at work, especially at laboratory Excellent German language skills (at least C1) and good English language skills (at least B2/C1) Strong communication and teamwork skills, a highly organized and structured approach to work, and a passion for working with students Desirable Practical experience with learning platforms (e.g. Moodle) and digital teaching/laboratory resources Pedagogical and didactic qualifications (e.g. a certificate in university teaching methodology) and experience with competence-based assessment What we offer: Work-Life-Balance : Our employees enjoy flexible working hours, remote/hybrid and/or part-time work (upon agreement). Inspiring working atmosphere: You are a part of an international academic team with excellent research infrastructure, dedicated colleagues and students who want to learn from you. Good public transport connections: Your workplace in the center of beautiful Vienna is easily accessible by public transport. Internal further training & coaching: Opportunity to deepen your skills on an ongoing basis. There are over 600 courses to choose from – free of charge. Fair salary: The basic salary of EUR 5.014,30 (on a fulltime basis) increases if we can credit professional experience. Equal opportunities for all: We welcome every additional/new personality to the team! It is that easy to apply: Your CV, including a list of publications (including research projects) A covering letter A brief teaching proposal (max. 2 pages) for biochemistry laboratory practical course A list of courses taught Certificate confirming completion of a doctoral/PhD degree Optional: teaching evaluations, examples of digital teaching materials, references Via our  job portal/ Apply now -  button If you have any questions, please contact: Petra Rust petra.rust@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection ​Application deadline: 11/06/2026 (Senior) Lecturer & Researcher Apply now » Find similar jobs: Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies, (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E), (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to 