    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-assistant-predoctoral-Vienna-Network-for-Atmospheric-Research-%28VINAR%29/1447669433/": {
      "title": "University assistant predoctoral",
      "description": "University assistant predoctoral - Vienna Network for Atmospheric Research (VINAR) Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » University assistant predoctoral - Vienna Network for Atmospheric Research (VINAR) The University of Vienna is a community of almost 11,000 individuals, including approximately 7,700 academic staff members, who passionately pursue answers to the profound questions that shape our future. They represent individuals driven by curiosity and a relentless pursuit of excellence. With us, they find the space to try things out and unfold their potential. Are you inspired by their passion and determination? We are currently seeking a/an University assistant predoctoral - Vienna Network for Atmospheric Research (VINAR) 51 Faculty of Physics Job vacancy starting: 11/01/2026 | Working hours:  30.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc) Limited contract until: 10/31/2030 Job ID: 6233 Are you interested in experimental aerosol physics, in-situ measurements, and both laboratory and field work? If so, join the Aerosol Physics and Environmental Physics (AEP) Group to investigate understudied aerosol components across urban and remote environments. As a pre-doc, you will be part of the AEP Group around Professor Bernadett Weinzierl. The AEP Group combines highly sophisticated laboratory, ground-based and aircraft measurements with innovative modelling to study the fundamental physical and chemical properties of aerosol particles and clouds. Current research covers various areas of aerosol science and spans the whole size spectrum from the nano- to the microscale. We are looking for a motivated pre-doctoral scientist to extend our team. The employment duration is 4 years. Your personal sphere of influence: As a pre-doc university assistant in this 4-year position, you will be part of the Aerosol Physics and Environmental Physics Group around Professor Bernadett Weinzierl. The overall aim of this position is the characterization of the atmospheric aerosol collected at the Aerosols Observatory of the University of Vienna, which is in the process of becoming a National Facility within the pan-European Aerosol, Clouds and Trace Gases Research Infrastructure ACTRIS, and comparison to the aerosol data measured at the Sonnblick Observatory, Austria. Specifically, you will focus on the determination of optical and microphysical properties of atmospheric aerosols measured at these two stations, one representing urban background environment, and the other one, remote atmosphere at 3100 m in altitude. The position is offered within the Vienna Network for Atmospheric Research (VINAR) and involves collaboration with colleagues at GeoSphere Austria and the Department of Meteorology and Geophysics at the Faculty of Earth Sciences, Geography and Astronomy, University of Vienna. The employment duration is 4 years. Initially limited to 1.5 years, the employment relationship is automatically extended to 4 years if the employer does not terminate it within the first 12 months by submitting a nonextension declaration. Your future tasks: Active participation in research, teaching & administration, which means: You will be involved in unique research projects in which we collaborate with top scientific institutions Your work will focus on rarely-studied aerosol components (including microplastics and others) at urban and remote sites in the framework of ACTRIS and beyond You will set up, characterize, maintain and operate ACTRIS instrumentation such as Aethalometer (AE), Nephelometer, Aerodynamic Particle Sizer (APS) in order to measure the aerosol microphysical and optical properties sampling from a PM10 inlet at the Aerosol Observatory You will characterize instruments in the laboratory, perform aerosol measurements at the Aerosol Observatory, process, analyze and interpret the aerosol data with respect to aerosol microphysical and optical properties You will compare data obtained at the Aerosol Observatory (urban background) in Vienna and the Sonnblick Observatory (remote atmosphere) You will collaborate within VINAR, GeoSphere Austria (Sonnblick Observatory) and the Department of Meteorology and Geophysics at the Faculty of Earth Sciences, Geography and Astronomy, University of Vienna (FLEXPART modelling) You will work on your dissertation and towards its completion in time. You will present your research plan to the faculty and complete a dissertation agreement within 12–18 months. This will be reviewed and adapted on an annual basis You will actively and continuously perform literature search to independently locate relevant journal articles You will contribute to teaching (lab courses, exercise classes) within the provisions of the collective bargaining agreement You will fill some administrative tasks, contributing to the success and self-organization of the group for research, teaching and administration You will contribute to outreach by publications, conference presentations and public activities This is part of your personality: Compulsory: Master's degree (or equivalent) in physics and/or aerosol-related topics such as atmospheric sciences, aerosol chemistry, meteorology, or similar Affinity for practical work; ideally, you have experience in experimental/technical work An excellent command of written and spoken English (C1 or higher) Experience in programming (e.g., Python) to perform your data analysis Reliable, regular presence in the laboratory on site in Vienna Willingness to travel: measurement campaigns may involve fieldwork away from the office, including national and international stays You are a team player with good social/communication skills, as the goal will only be achieved in a team Class B driving license Desirable: Knowledge in atmospheric and/or aerosol physics and experimental work Experience with common aerosol particle detection and characterization techniques, in particular with measurements of aerosol microphysical and optical properties, is considered an asset Experience in building experimental setups, instrument characterization, and calibration Experience with in-field measurement campaigns is an asset Initiative in finding solutions for technical and scientific problems What we offer: Inspiring working atmosphere: You are a part of an international academic team in a healthy and fair working environment. Good public transport connections: Your workplace in the center of beautiful Vienna is easily accessible by public transport. Potential for development : Success in life depends on what you make of it, but if you are ambitious and successful, there are plenty of opportunities to connect you to many relevant top research groups in the world. Internal further training & coaching: Opportunity to deepen your skills on an ongoing basis. There are over 600 courses to choose from – free of charge. Fair salary: The basic salary of EUR 3,776.10 (full-time basis, 14x p.a.) increases if we can credit professional experience. The duration of employment is 4 years . Initially limited to 1.5 years, the employment relationship is automatically extended to 4 years if the employer does not terminate it within the first 12 months by submitting a non-extension declaration. Equal opportunities for all: We welcome every additional/new personality to the team! It is that easy to apply: With your scientific curriculum vitae. A summary of your previous academic and research achievements. A short statement on your research interests for the future. Your Bachelor’s and Master’s degree: an excellent academic degree is a good entrance statement for this position. Note that while a Master’s degree is the usual legal prerequisite for a PhD position at the University of Vienna, we can consider Bachelor’s degrees (preferentially with Honors) in exceptional cases, too. If you have any questions, please contact: Bernadett Weinzierl bernadett.weinzierl@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities, the advancement of women and diversity. We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection ​Application deadline: 10/24/2026 Prae Doc Apply now » Find similar jobs: predoctoral, Praedoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cooki