    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-assistant-predoctoral/1435337633/": {
      "title": "University assistant predoctoral",
      "description": "University assistant predoctoral Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » University assistant predoctoral The University of Vienna is a community of almost 11,000 individuals, including approximately 7,700 academic staff members, who passionately pursue answers to the profound questions that shape our future. They represent individuals driven by curiosity and a relentless pursuit of excellence. With us, they find the space to try things out and unfold their potential. Are you inspired by their passion and determination? We are currently seeking a/an University assistant predoctoral 50 Faculty of Life Sciences Job vacancy starting: 04/01/2027 | Working hours:  30.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc) Limited contract until: Job ID: 6181 Explore and teach at the University of Vienna, where more than 7,500 academics thrive on curiosity in continuous exploration and help us better understand our world. Does this sound like you? Then join our accomplished team! Your personal sphere of influence: The Department of Behavioral and Cognitive Biology is looking for a university assistant predoctoral to join the research group of Prof. Narly Golestani (Brain and Language Lab). The position is limited to 3 years with the possibility of extending for a further year. The Brain and Language Lab investigates the neurobiological foundations of language and auditory processing, with a particular focus on individual differences, multilingual and multiliterate experience, language aptitude, dyslexia, brain anatomy and experience-dependent plasticity. Our research combines structural and functional neuroimaging, EEG/MEG, behavioural methods, computational modelling, automated neuroanatomical phenotyping, machine learning and advanced statistical approaches. The doctoral project will be developed jointly with the successful candidate and tailored to their methodological background, previous research experience and scientific interests within the broader research areas of the lab. Possible projects may draw on our existing multimodal adult datasets, including the NEBULA101 dataset and associated unpublished data from adults with and without dyslexia. Potential research questions include: How multilingual and multiliterate experience, language aptitude and dyslexia relate to brain structure, activation and connectivity. How neural systems supporting visual word-form processing, spoken language, music and spatial navigation are organised and interrelated. Whether individual differences in memory, auditory processing, executive control and navigation reveal markers of risk, resilience or compensatory mechanisms associated with dyslexia. Depending on the research question and the successful candidate’s expertise, the project may combine MRI, EEG/MEG, behavioural assessment, computational modelling and automated neuroanatomical phenotyping. The successful candidate will also become a member of the Vienna Doctoral School in Cognition, Behaviour and Neuroscience (CoBeNe), which provides interdisciplinary doctoral training and opportunities for scientific exchange across psychology, neuroscience, behavioural biology and related disciplines. Further information about the Brain and Language Lab is available at: https://www.brainandlanguagelab.org Your future tasks: The successful candidate will participate in the Department’s research, teaching—to the extent regulated by the collective bargaining agreement—and administration. This involves: Developing, conducting and completing a doctoral research project within the research areas described above. Finalising the dissertation agreement within 12–18 months. Analysing behavioural and neuroscientific data and developing transparent and reproducible analysis workflows. Participating in research projects and scientific studies conducted within the Brain and Language Lab. Preparing international scientific publications and presenting research findings at national and international conferences. Participating in the activities and training programme of the Vienna Doctoral School in Cognition, Behaviour and Neuroscience. Independently teaching courses in accordance with the provisions of the collective bargaining agreement. Supervising students, where appropriate. Participating in evaluation measures and quality assurance. Contributing to departmental administration and to teaching and research administration. This is part of your personality: A completed Master’s degree or equivalent in psychology, biomedical engineering, cognitive neuroscience, neuroscience, cognitive science, computer science, data science, physics or another relevant discipline. Applicants from other disciplinary backgrounds are welcome provided that their subsequent training and research experience demonstrate substantial preparation in cognitive neuroscience and quantitative methods. Research experience in cognitive neuroscience, including experience working with empirical behavioural and/or neuroscientific data. Strong programming skills relevant to scientific data analysis, demonstrated through substantive experience with at least one programming language such as Python, R, MATLAB or a comparable language. A strong background in statistics and quantitative research methods, including practical experience applying statistical methods to empirical data. Experience with experimental design, data processing and the interpretation of complex datasets. Experience in scientific writing and research methods, for example through the completion of an empirical Master’s thesis. Excellent command of written and spoken English. The ability to work both independently and collaboratively. Strong organisational, communication and problem-solving skills. A strong motivation to complete a doctoral dissertation and contribute actively to the research and teaching activities of the lab and department. Desirable qualifications Practical experience with one or more cognitive-neuroscience methods, particularly structural or functional MRI, EEG or MEG. Experience with neuroimaging analysis, functional or structural connectivity, computational morphometry or signal processing. Experience with multivariate statistics, machine learning or computational modelling. Familiarity with Linux, high-performance computing, version control and reproducible research practices. Previous research on language, reading, auditory processing, multilingualism, individual differences or dyslexia. Experience in teaching, student supervision or research communication. Knowledge of German or a willingness to acquire German-language skills is desirable but not required. What we offer: Work-life balance: Our employees enjoy flexible working hours and can partially work remotely. Inspiring working atmosphere: You are a part of an international academic team in a healthy and fair working environment. Good public transport connections: Your workplace is easily accessible by public transport. Internal further training & Coaching: Opportunity to deepen your skills on an ongoing basis. There are over 600 courses to choose from – free of charge. Fair salary: The basic salary of EUR 3.776,10 (on a full-time basis) increases if we can credit professional experience. Equal opportunities for all: We welcome every additional/new personality to the team! The employment duration is 3 years . Initially limited to 1.5 years, the employment relationship is automatically extended to 3 years if the employer does not terminate it within the first 12 months by submitting a declaration of non-extension. With appropriate work progress, an extension to a total maximum of 4 years is possible. It is that easy to apply: Please submit the following documents in English: A letter of motivation, including a summary of your research interests; a brief description of your relevant experience in cognitive neuroscience, programming and statistical analysis; and the names and contact details of three referees (maximum two pages). A scientific curriculum vitae, including publications, conference contributions and teaching experience, if available. Your Master’s degree certificate or proof that the degree will be completed before the position begins. Your transcript of records. Via the University of Vienna job portal using the “Apply now” button. If you have any questions, please contact: Narly Golestani narly.golestani@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection ​Application deadline: 02/01/2027 Prae Doc Apply now » Find similar jobs: predoctoral, Praedoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing, and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled AddThis Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider AddThis Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
