    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-Assistant-postdoctoral/1453340933/": {
      "title": "University Assistant postdoctoral",
      "description": "University Assistant postdoctoral Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » The University of Vienna has been ranked among the Top 100 Universities in the World by Times Higher Education (THE). We strive to create a harmony of contrasts, creating new possibilities and ideas. Let us shape the future together and make a real difference to society. We are looking for a University Assistant postdoctoral 91 Centre for Microbiology and Environmental Systems Science Job vacancy starting: 01/01/2027 | Working hours: 40.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 lit. b (postdoc) Limited contract until: Job ID: 6398 The Centre for Microbiology and Environmental Systems Science (CeMESS) at the University of Vienna conducts basic research on the structure and function of microbiomes at an internationally leading level. We are looking for a post postdoctoral researcher to support our team. Your personal sphere of influence: The Division of Microbiology and Ecosystem Science (DoME, https://dome.univie.ac.at/) is seeking a highly motivated postdoctoral researcher to join our group. The candidate will focus on investigating metabolic features that may shape interactions of Patescibacteria with other microbes including polyphosphate-accumulating organisms in wastewater treatment plants. This research aims to elucidate the nature of interactions between these microbes and their potential implication for wastewater treatment processes. Our group is dedicated to exploring various aspects of microbial ecology in both natural and engineered systems, including wastewater treatment. Your future tasks: The postdoctoral researcher will investigate the interactions between Patescibacteria and polyphosphate-accumulating organisms in wastewater treatment plants aiming to uncover novel aspects of this fascinating interplay. This work will primarily involve bioinformatic analyses, including large-scale genome and metagenome data interpretation, complemented by lab-based approaches, such as fluorescence in situ hybridization and activity-based assays to validate findings and explore functional insights. This is part of your personality: •    Experience in population and co-occurrence analyses as well comparative genomic analyses for metabolic reconstruction. •    Experience in using a range of bioinformatical tools but also lab-based methods to study microbial interactions. •    In-depth understanding of Patescibacteria and knowledge of microbial processes in wastewater treatment systems, including phosphorus removal and polyphosphate-accumulating organisms. •    Experience in molecular techniques like fluorescence in situ hybridization and PCR-based methods. •    Phd in a relevant field What we offer: Work-Life-Balance: Our employees enjoy flexible, family-friendly working hours, remote/hybrid and/or part-time work (upon agreement). Inspiring working atmosphere: You are part of an international academic team in a healthy and fair working environment. Good public transport connections: Your workplace in the center of beautiful Vienna is easily accessible by public transport. Internal further training & coaching: Opportunity to deepen your skills on an ongoing basis. There are over 600 courses to choose from – free of charge. Fair salary: The basic gross salary of EUR 5.014,30 (on full-time basis, 14x per year) increases if we can credit professional experience. Equal opportunities for everyone: We look forward to diverse personalities in the team. It is that easy to apply: •    Your application should consist of a letter of motivation (1-2 pages), the letter of motivation should address the stated qualifications for the position, relevant experience and research interests •    your CV including a publication list, university certificate(s) including grades and contact information of two references. •    Via our job portal / Apply now - button For any content-related questions, please contact: Annina Müller Strassnig annina.mueller@univie.ac.at The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Jobs for personalities Data protection Application deadline: 11/11/2026 Post Doc Apply now » Find similar jobs: postdoctoral, Postdoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie 