    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/PhD-Position-Analyzing-Polymer-Degradation-by-Soil-Enzymes/1453458833/": {
      "title": "PhD Position: Analyzing Polymer Degradation by Soil Enzymes",
      "description": "PhD Position: Analyzing Polymer Degradation by Soil Enzymes Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » The University of Vienna has been ranked among the Top 100 Universities in the World by Times Higher Education (THE). We strive to create a harmony of contrasts, creating new possibilities and ideas. Let us shape the future together and make a real difference to society. We are offering a PhD Position: Analyzing Polymer Degradation by Soil Enzymes 91 Centre for Microbiology and Environmental Systems Science Job vacancy starting: 03/01/2027 or soon thereafter | Working hours: 40.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc) Limited contract until: 02/29/2028 | The contract will initially be limited to one year, with the aim to extend to three years. Job ID: 6419 Do you want to conduct basic research that can inform solutions for sustainable agriculture? Join our group ( EDGE ) at the University of Vienna as a PhD student within the MSCA Doctoral Network Agripolys and apply environmental analytical chemistry to investigate the enzymatic degradation of polymers in agricultural soils. Your personal sphere of influence: Polymers are important for numerous agricultural applications. To avoid the accumulation of polymers in soils and other environmental systems, soil biodegradability is a key desired feature for many polymers. To inform the development of soil biodegradable polymers, a fundamental understanding of the activity and specificity of soil enzymes is needed. Rooted in environmental analytical chemistry (centered around high-resolution mass spectrometry), this project (Agripolys DC6) aims to decipher biodegradation pathways of several promising polymer classes and thereby shine light on the degradation potential of soil enzymes. Our research group is part of the Centre for Microbiology and Environmental Systems Science ( CeMESS ) at the University of Vienna, Austria. We are dedicated to conducting cutting-edge research at the intersection of (bio)chemistry, microbiology, and environmental science. Your future tasks: You actively participate in research & administration, which means: development and completion of a dissertation within the scope of the research project AGRIPOLYS; participation in the research project AGRIPOLYS through experiments and the development of analytical methods; publication and presentation of research in international journal and conferences; contribution to administrative tasks in research and administration. Being part of the VDS MES doctoral school, we expect the successful candidate to sign a doctoral thesis agreement within 12-18 months. This is part of your personality: A master’s degree in analytical chemistry, polymer chemistry, biochemistry, environmental chemistry, food chemistry, microbiology, or a closely related field. Laboratory experience in one or several of the above research fields is a strong asset. Fluent in spoken and written English (level C1). High motivation, independence, and reliability. Mobility rule: Applicants must not have resided or carried out their main activity (work, studies, etc.) in Austria for more than 12 months during the 36 months immediately preceding the recruitment date. What we offer: A supportive and stimulating working environment and excellent laboratory facilities; A fully funded position (full funding for 3 years) in accordance with the collective bargaining agreement (basic salary of EUR 3776,10 on a full-time basis); Scientific collaboration and secondments within and beyond the project network; A chance to live and work in Vienna – renowned for its high quality of life. It is that easy to apply: Your complete application contains: your CV, including contact details of at least two referees, your BSc and MSc transcripts, and your letter of motivation that specifies your fit to the position. Only application submitted via our job portal jobs.univie.ac.at (Apply now-button) will be considered. For any content-related questions, please contact: Stella Maria Spanlang edge.cemess@univie.ac.at The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Jobs for personalities Data protection Application deadline: 11/30/2026 [[filter3]] [[custAlternativeApplyURL]] Apply now » Find similar jobs: predoctoral, Praedoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing, and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled AddThis Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider AddThis Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
