    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/Senior-Lecturer-%28academic-and-instructional-teaching%29/1452526433/": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer (academic and instructional teaching)",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer  (academic and instructional teaching) Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Senior Lecturer  (academic and instructional teaching) At the University of Vienna, almost 11,000 people work together on the big questions of the future. Approximately 7,700 of them are academic staff members. These are individuals who, with their curiosity and their continuous pursuit of excellence, engage in international cutting-edge research and teaching. With us, you will also find space to unfold your potential. We are looking for a/an ... Senior Lecturer  (academic and instructional teaching) 53 Faculty of Earth Sciences, Geography and Astronomy Job vacancy starting: 02/01/2027 | Working hours:  20.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 lit. b (postdoc) Limited contract until: 01/31/2031 Job ID: 6281 In case of positive evaluation at the end of the fixed-term period of 4 years, the position will be changed to a permanet position. Do you enjoy working with young people, are you curious, and do you want to pass on your knowledge?  As a Senior Lecturer, you play a crucial role in educating students. In addition to providing a solid academic education, we also place a special emphasis on the personal development of students. We support students in developing a curious and critical thinking, thereby creating a solid foundation for the professional challenges of the next generation. The position combines academic and instructional teaching for a total of 8.5 hours. Your workplace: The Senior Lecturer position is based at the Department of Geology (Institut für Geology / IfG) within the Faculty of Earth Sciences, Geography, and Astronomy. With more than 30 academic staff and over 300 students, the IfG offers an inspiring environment for conducting excellent basic research and addressing pressing societal challenges through research and teaching. The position is part of the Structural Geology and Tectonics research group. The members of the research group investigate how, why, and at what rate rocks deform under tectonic influence. To analyze the response to tectonic forces, macroscopic structures such as folds, shear zones, and faults are quantitatively mapped in the field. In addition, rocks are examined using high-resolution analytical methods to understand deformation processes. The application of numerical models helps to better understand the physical processes of rock deformation. As Senior Lecturer, your teaching responsibilities will primarily involve instructing students in general geoscientific and mathematical-geological methods such as modeling and their practical applications particularly in quantitative structural geology, tectonics, geo-energy, and mineral resources geology, as well as conducting field instruction, especially in mountainous terrain. Your tasks: You will independently conduct and lead courses at the bachelor’s and master’s levels in accordance with the provisions of the collective bargaining agreement. The 20-hour-per-week work schedule includes an average teaching load of 5 semester-weekly hours of academic teaching and 3.5 semester-weekly hours of instructional teaching. You will perform administrative tasks, particularly in the area of teaching administration. We expect you to keep up to date with the latest scientifc developments and to engage in didactic training, especially during lecture-free periods. Preconditions for an application: We are looking for individuals who see university teaching as an interesting and challenging career path. Preconditions for an application resp. terms of admission: Completed doctoral degree in Earth Sciences/Geology Several years of independent teaching experience at a postsecondary educational institution Excellent didactic skills and passion for sharing knowledge and for university teaching In-depth knowledge of geological methods, particularly quantitative methods and practical field-based and applied geology Excellent command of German and English You are a team player with strong interpersonal and communication skills. What we offer: Inspiring work environment: You’ll be part of an international team with excellent research infrastructure, dedicated colleagues, and students eager to learn from you. Good public transportation access: Your new workplace is easily accessible by public transportation. In-house training and coaching: We offer you ongoing opportunities to expand and deepen your skills. Fair salary: The base salary of EUR 5,079.50 (based on full-time employment - 40h per week / amount as of 01.01.2027) increases if we can take your professional experience into account. Equal opportunities for all: We welcome every new member to our team! It is that easy to apply: CV and certificates Certificate of a completed doctoral program in Earth Sciences List of courses taught (evaluation results, if available) Letter of motivation (max. 2 pages) Didactic teaching concept (max. 2 pages) List of publications and list of research projects completed Via our job portal / “Apply Now” button If you have any questions, please contact: Daniel Le Heron daniel.le-heron@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection ​Application deadline: 11/24/2026 (Senior) Lecturer & Researcher Apply now » Find similar jobs: Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies, (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E), (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing,