    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-assistant-%28predoctoral%29-at-the-Department-of-Political-Science/1455578533/": {
      "title": "University assistant (predoctoral)",
      "description": "University assistant (predoctoral) at the Department of Political Science Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » At the University of Vienna almost 11,000 personalities work together towards answering the big questions of the future. Around 7,700  of them do research and teaching, around 3,000 work in administration and organisation. We are looking for a University assistant (predoctoral) at the Department of Political Science 49 Faculty of Social Sciences Job vacancy starting: 03/01/2027 | Working hours: 30.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc) Limited contract until: 02/28/2031 Job ID: 6369 The announcement is made for four years, whereby the employment relationship is initially limited to 1.5 years and is automatically extended to a total of four years, unless the employer submits a declaration of non-renewal after a maximum of 12 months. Your future workplace: Your future place is at the Department of Political Science, in the research areas Comparative Politics and Migration. The Department of Political Science, a subunit of the Faculty of Social Sciences, addresses all major fields of political science. It is dedicated to innovative and problem-oriented research and provides students with a wide range of specialisations. Members of the Department study the transformation of governance, statehood and democracy across different policy areas, geographical regions and political areas. As a predoctoral university assistant, you will work at the intersection of Comparative Political Science (Univ. Prof. Bohle) and International Migration and Mobility (Ass. Prof. Hadj Abdou). We are particularly interested in questions of political economy as they relate to international migration and mobility. Thus, your work may focus on policy regimes, policies, instruments, mechanisms, and practices, as well as different actors in the realm of labor migration and the labor market integration of immigrant groups. The (ethical) recruitment, retention, and inclusion of so-called international talent fall within the scope of possible topics, as do various aspects of exclusion and marginalization. The regional focus of the research is not limited to any particular region or level; it can cover different countries and regions of origin as well as destination regions/countries (including Austria) as well as various levels (global, regional, national, subnational). Your future tasks: You will actively participate in research, teaching, and administration in the research areas Comparative Politics and Migration, which means: You will work on your political science dissertation in the field of labor migration We expect you to finalize your dissertation agreement within 12–18 months Participation in research projects and scholarly studies Contribution to publications and presentations Participation in project proposals and the acquisition of external funding Supervision of students You will independently teach courses in accordance with the provisions of the collective bargaining agreement Participation in the organisation of meetings, conferences, symposia Participation in the department administration as well as in teaching and research administration Requirements: A completed master’s or diploma degree in political science or a related field, ideally with a specialization in migration, political economy, or labor Expertise in the field of international migration Proven experience in academic writing and qualitative research methods, proficiency in quantitative methods is a plus Applied computer skills Excellent English skills (C1) / knowledge of another foreign language (C1) if relevant to the dissertation topic You are a team player with strong social and communication skills The following criteria are desirable: Teaching experience / experience with e-learning Experience of living abroad Knowledge of university processes and structures Command of German What we offer: Work-life balance: You have flexible working hours and can partially work remotely. Inspiring working atmosphere: You are a part of an international academic team with excellent research infrastructure. Good public transport connections: Your new workplace is easily accessible by public transport. Internal further training & Coaching: We continually offer you the opportunity to expand and deepen your skills. Choose from a selection of over 600 free workshops each year. Fair salary: The basic salary of EUR 3.836,10 (on a full-time basis) increases if we can credit professional experience. Get off to a great start in your new job: the Welcome Compass helps you settle into your new role at the University of Vienna and life in Vienna. Equal opportunities for all: We welcome every new personality to the team! Requested application material: Letter of motivation, explaining how you would contribute to the Department of Political Science and strengthen research on migration and labor at the department Resume, including a list of publications (if applicable) Dissertation proposal (max. 4 pages, plus a maximum of one separate page for the bibliography), including a 1,000-character abstract at the beginning. The proposal must clearly articulate the connection to the topics of migration and labor, the relevance of the specific topic, and the expected contribution to political science, as well as the analytical methodology and approach, including research-guiding assumptions or hypotheses Proof of completion of a master’s or diploma degree Contact information for a reference Via our job portal / Apply now-button If you have any content questions, please contact: Univ. Prof. Dorothee Bohle dorothee.bohle@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of  Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection Application deadline: 11/30/2026 Prae Doc Apply now » Find similar jobs: predoctoral, Praedoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing, and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled AddThis Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider AddThis Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
